    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0945" n="821" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg821"/>

                <head>No. 488.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay
                        to Señor Navarro.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-12-22"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 22,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to your note of the 28th of
                    August last,<anchor n="†" xml:id="d492-f1"/> I have now <pb facs="0946" n="822"
                        xml:id="pg822"/> the honor to inclose, for the information of your
                    government, a copy of a letter recently received from his excellency the
                    governor of Texas, with its accompaniment, touching the complaint of the
                    governor of the State of Chihuahua, respecting one Robert Martin and others,
                    accused of committing outrages on both frontiers.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN HAY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d492-a1.xml" xpointer="d492-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d492-a2.xml" xpointer="d492-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
